class_name CharacterStories
extends RefCounted
## The long stories shown in Collection when you tap a character you own
## (character select keeps the short description). GM's and Ashiela's are
## their own letters.

const STORIES := {
	"proktoy": "Every neighborhood has one kid who is always \"it\", and around here that kid is Proktoy. Nobody remembers the first game of tumbang preso he lost, only that he has been the taya ever since, guarding the can with his headband pulled low and his eyes wide open. People say he doesn't blink because he's afraid of missing the moment someone sneaks a throw.\n\nBeing chased every single afternoon turned him into the fastest runner on the street. He knows every alley, every loose fence board and every corner store that will let him hide behind the counter. When the other kids finally started picking him first for their team, he pretended not to care, but he walked home grinning that day.\n\nHe is the first friend you make in Tumbang Henyo, and the one who never leaves the court. Win or lose, he'll be there tomorrow at five, wild hair and all, asking for one more round.",
	"kei": "Kei never rushes. She ties her long hair back slowly, picks her slipper slowly, and answers questions only after reading every choice twice. The other kids used to tease her for it, until they noticed she almost never gets one wrong.\n\nHer secret is patience. While everyone else sprints the moment the can falls, Kei waits for the taya to commit, then slips out the other side. She is somehow always the first one home before the streetlights turn on, sitting on her doorstep with a cold soft drink, watching the rest of the gang scramble.\n\nHer grandmother says she has an old soul. Kei just says that the game is easier when you stop and look at it for a second.",
	"lisa": "You hear Lisa before you see her. The moment a slipper connects with the can, a voice cuts across the whole neighborhood: \"DOWN!\" Half the neighborhood turns around to look, and the other half already knows it's her.\n\nHer curly pink hair goes everywhere, but the yellow star clip on top never moves an inch. She says it's her lucky charm and that it has never once fallen off, not even when she tripped into a canal chasing a stray throw. She came out soaked and laughing, star still perfectly in place.\n\nLisa keeps the score in her head for every game, remembers everyone's best throw, and will remind you about your worst one for the next three weeks. She is loud, loyal and impossible to stay mad at.",
	"badette": "Badette doesn't walk onto the court, he arrives. Pink hair styled to perfection, outfit coordinated down to the slippers, and a dramatic hair flip before every single throw. \"Oh, gorgeous!\" he shouts whenever anyone makes a good shot, including himself, especially himself.\n\nThe other kids thought he'd be all show until the first time the can went flying across the street. He runs like the court is a runway and dodges like he's practiced it in front of a mirror, which, to be fair, he has. His slipper throws come with commentary, a pose and sometimes a curtsy.\n\nEveryone in the neighborhood knows two things about Badette: he will hype you up louder than anyone when you're down, and he will absolutely judge your outfit while doing it. The gang wouldn't have it any other way.",
	"migo": "Migo talks so little that some kids thought he couldn't. Black shirt, black shorts, bandana tied tight, he shows up, nods once, and waits for the game to start. When someone asks him a question, he usually just points at the right answer.\n\nWhat he lacks in words he makes up for in aim. Migo has hit the can from distances that started arguments and ended friendships. He doesn't celebrate; he just turns around and walks to the line while everyone else is still shouting about it.\n\nRumor has it he practices alone at dawn with an old pair of slippers and a dented can behind his house. He has never confirmed it. He has never denied it either.",
	"saisai": "Sai Sai's hair reaches all the way to her knees, bright blue with a red ribbon you can spot from the other end of the court. She looks like she stepped out of a storybook, and every new kid makes the mistake of thinking she'll be easy to beat.\n\nThey learn quickly. Behind the sweet smile is the most competitive player in the neighborhood. She remembers every loss, plans every comeback and has a way of appearing right behind the taya just as they turn around. When she wins, she says \"thank you for the game\" so politely that it somehow stings more.\n\nHer friends call her the storm in a ribbon. She takes it as a compliment.",
	"gm": "My one and only pale blue star,\n\nSince we first met seven years ago, I have never fully understood the circumstances that led me to you. Our story has always felt surreal and, in some ways, wonderfully absurd. These unexpected and unpredictable circumstances have become part of what makes our connection so extraordinary. Over time, we have learned not to dwell on the past, for we must leave room for the future. We have been given the opportunity to love and grow in the present, and I hope we will continue to make the most of this precious gift as we build a love that reaches toward infinity.\n\nI may sometimes worry about the things left unsaid and the uncertainties that the future may bring. Nevertheless, I want you to know that you will always be my guiding light, my bastion, and the stronghold of my faith. You have inspired me to believe in things I once struggled to understand, and through your presence, you have given my life a renewed sense of purpose. You have taught me the importance of devotion, patience, and sincerity in loving another person. Above all, you have reminded me that love is not simply a feeling to be experienced, but a commitment to be upheld through time, distance, uncertainty, and change.\n\nYou have become someone I wish to love for as long as time permits, and perhaps even beyond the limits of time itself. Who can truly say when time will end, or whether the very concept of eternity will one day cease to exist? What I know is that, for as long as I am able, I will continue to choose you. My loyalty to you shall remain steadfast, and my affection shall not be measured by the passing of days or months. Whatever the future holds, I hope we will continue to face it together, allowing our love to mature and deepen with every experience we share.\n\nSincerely, the Ghost.",
	"ashiela": "My one and only savior,\n\nThis may sound rather cheesy, but I genuinely mean every word. You are the reason I have changed for the better, helping me grow from someone who once struggled to understand herself into a better version of who I am today. You have brought sunlight into my life when I felt as though I was being pulled into an abyss. If I were to describe you, I would say that you are the dawn in the middle of a restless night. You are my one and only sacred gem, my purest love, and the sweetest green flag I have ever known. I cannot imagine my life without you, GM. I hope you will always treat me with the same love and sincerity that I have for you, because this is how deeply I have fallen for you.\n\nOnce again, I love you, GM.\n\nHonestly, you are the first person who has ever brought tears to my eyes, not out of anger or sadness, but because of the overwhelming joy, concern, and love I feel for you. I love you so much that the thought of seeing you smile at another girl makes me feel a little jealous. I am only joking, of course. You are free to smile at anyone you speak to, and I would never want to take that simple happiness away from you. All I want is to love you sincerely, to see you happy, and to continue growing alongside you. You have become someone truly special to me, and I hope that what we share will continue to grow into something even more beautiful with time.\n\nSincerely, The Acre.",
}


static func of(id: String) -> String:
	return STORIES.get(id, "")
